      "core_pillar": "",
      "style": "Act I: The GroundingDichotomy of ControlTrack 03 of 13Tempo: Mid-tempo, steady, reliable rhythm03. Just My Own Two Hands Grounded Country Blues, Americana Folk \u2022 Mood: Resolute, Calm, Centered, PurposefulOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "tempo": "Act I: The GroundingDichotomy of ControlTrack 03 of 13 Mid-tempo, steady, reliable rhythm03. Just My Own Two HandsStyle: Grounded Country Blues, Americana Folk \u2022 Mood: Resolute, Calm, Centered, PurposefulOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "quote": "But I can't steer this mighty ship\nOr heal the world with words I've said\nI can't un-poison every sip\nOr fix the path that lies ahead",
      "story": "\"Just My Own Two Hands\" is the practical heart of the album's first act, a direct musical embodiment of the Stoic Dichotomy of Control. The song tells the story of a craftsman or blue-collar worker feeling overwhelmed by the relentless chaos of the modern world\u2014political shouting, economic instability, and endless bad news. He finds his salvation not by trying to solve the world's problems, but by deliberately narrowing his focus to what is within his immediate power: his work, his integrity, and the tangible results of his own effort. Set to a steady, reliable country-blues rhythm, the track is a calming anthem for finding peace and purpose amidst turmoil by anchoring oneself to the tangible and controllable.\n\nClean Acoustic Guitar, simple bass line, gentle brush-stick drums \u2022 Male, Clear, Calm, Centered, Baritone\n\nGrounded Country Blues with an Americana folk feel. A steady, reliable mid, rhythmic acoustic guitar. The mood is calm, centered, and purposeful. A clear and resolute lead male baritone sings with simple, honest conviction.\n\nIn a world deafened by political shouting and global anxieties, where can we find peace? This song answers with the Dichotomy of Control. The narrator, a craftsman, deliberately turns away from the chaos of the screen to focus on the wood and tools on his bench. It is a tribute to the sanity found in doing good work within your own small sphere of influence.\n\n\n    \n\n\n@TheShadyRiverBard",
      "clean_lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nThe screen is on, the shouting starts\nAbout some bill I'll never read\nThe talking heads all play their parts\nTo plant a different kind of seed\nOf worry 'bout some foreign shore\nOf fear about the coming years\nAnd I don't know what I'm angry for\nBut I can feel the rising fears\n\n[Chorus]\nBut I can't steer this mighty ship\nOr heal the world with words I've said\nI can't un-poison every sip\nOr fix the path that lies ahead\nThe only truth I understand\nIs held right here within my soul\nI'll do the good work that I can\nWith just my own two hands' control\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe headlines tell of rising tides\nThe market dips, the market soars\nA fragile peace somewhere abides\nWhile others fight in futile wars\nAnd I could let it drain my soul\nA ghost in my own house to be\nBut I've got a different goal\nTo focus on what's in front of me\n\n[Chorus]\n'Cause I can't steer this mighty ship\nOr heal the world with words I've said\nI can't un-poison every sip\nOr fix the path that lies ahead\nThe only truth I understand\nIs held right here within my soul\nI'll do the good work that I can\nWith just my own two hands' control\n\n[Bridge]\nThe smell of coffee, metal, wood\nThe simple, honest, clean-drawn line\nThis little patch of understood\nIs sacred, and it's truly mine\n\n[Chorus]\nNo, I can't steer this mighty ship\nOr heal the world with words I've said\nI can't un-poison every sip\nOr fix the path that lies ahead\nThe only truth I understand\nIs held right here within my soul\nI'll do the good work that I can\nWith just my own two hands' control\n\n[Outro]\nYeah, just my own two hands\nIt's all I understand\n\n\u00a9 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
