      "core_pillar": "",
      "style": "Act I: The GroundingDichotomy of ControlTrack 04 of 13Tempo: Very Slow, Sparse04. The Unseen Storm Intimate Contemplative Folk, Singer-Songwriter, Acoustic Ballad \u2022 Mood: Resolute, Defiant, Grounded, Unflinching, StoicOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "tempo": "Act I: The GroundingDichotomy of ControlTrack 04 of 13 Very Slow, Sparse04. The Unseen StormStyle: Intimate Contemplative Folk, Singer-Songwriter, Acoustic Ballad \u2022 Mood: Resolute, Defiant, Grounded, Unflinching, StoicOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "quote": "But that's an unseen storm out there\nA war that's happening outside my soul\nTheir words are only empty air\nA thing I never can control",
      "story": "\"The Unseen Storm\" concludes the first act of the album with a powerful and defiant take on the Dichotomy of Control. The song grapples with the emotional weight of unjust criticism and public opinion. Instead of finding a vulnerable, quiet peace, the narrator takes a resolute and unflinching stance. He recognizes the gossip and judgment as an external force he cannot control and makes a powerful declaration of his own integrity and character. Musically, the song creates a compelling contrast, setting a raw, powerful, and weathered vocal against a sparse, contemplative folk arrangement, embodying the concept of unshakeable inner strength amidst outer chaos.\n\nDelicate fingerpicked acoustic guitar \u2022 Male, Raw, Powerful chest voice, Weathered Baritone\n\nReputation is a thing we cannot control, yet we let it rule us. This song serves as a shield against the \"unseen storm\" of gossip and public opinion. The narrator recognizes that what others say is merely wind; his character is the only flame he needs to tend. A song for anyone who has ever felt the sting of a false word and chosen integrity over argument.\n\n\n    \n\n\n@TheShadyRiverBard",
      "clean_lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nThe whispers fall like freezing rain\nA bitter wind of \"have-you-heard\"\nYou feel the turning of the vane\nOn every careless, cutting word\nThey build a you that isn't you\nWith stones of envy and of doubt\nAnd there ain't a thing that you can do\nTo keep the rising water out\n\n[Chorus]\nBut that's an unseen storm out there\nA war that's happening outside my soul\nTheir words are only empty air\nA thing I never can control\nMy own true north is all I need\nThe quiet voice that knows my name\nLet them plant their bitter seed\nI'll tend my own small flame\n\n[Verse 2]\nYou want to scream, you want to fight\nCorrect the course of every lie\nAnd stand all day and through the night\nWith proof to show them how they're wrong and why\nBut you'd be arguing with the tide\nOr shouting sermons at the wind\nThere is no safer place to hide\nThan in the comfort of your own skin\n\n[Chorus]\n'Cause that's an unseen storm out there\nA war that's happening outside my soul\nTheir words are only empty air\nA thing I never can control\nMy own true north is all I need\nThe quiet voice that knows my name\nLet them plant their bitter seed\nI'll tend my own small flame\n\n[Bridge]\nThe thunder rolls, the winds may blow\nBut in this quiet room I find\nThe only truth I have to know\nIs I'm the master of my mind\n\n[Chorus]\nSo let the unseen storm rage on\nThat war is happening outside my soul\nTheir words are gone as quick as dawn\nA thing I never will control\nMy own true north is all I need\nThe quiet voice that knows my name\nLet them plant their bitter seed\nI'll tend my own small flame\n\n[Outro]\nMy own small flame.\n\n\u00a9 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
