      "style": "Act II: The ForgeThe Obstacle is the WayTrack 05 of 13Tempo: Mid-tempo, Driving Rhythm05. The Mason's Wall Gritty Blues Rock, Southern Rock, Americana Rock \u2022 Mood: Determined, Gritty, Powerful, Unrelenting, AnthemicOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "tempo": "Act II: The ForgeThe Obstacle is the WayTrack 05 of 13 Mid-tempo, Driving Rhythm05. The Mason's WallStyle: Gritty Blues Rock, Southern Rock, Americana Rock \u2022 Mood: Determined, Gritty, Powerful, Unrelenting, AnthemicOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "quote": "But this ain't the thing that blocks the path\nThis is the quarry and the stone\nIt ain't the focus of God's wrath\nIt's building me from skin and bone",
      "story": "Kicking off the album's second act, \"The Mason's Wall\" translates the Stoic principle \"The Obstacle is the Way\" into a powerful blues-rock anthem. The song uses the metaphor of a mason confronting an insurmountable wall to explore how life's greatest barriers are not merely impediments, but the very tools by which character is forged. The narrator moves from initial despair to embracing the struggle, realizing that the act of lifting each stone builds the strength needed to continue. The track's driving rhythm and gritty electric guitar mark a deliberate sonic shift for the album, embodying the heat, pressure, and transformative power of the forge.\n\nHeavy overdriven electric guitar riff, pounding drums, driving bassline \u2022 Male, Powerful, Raw, Soulful, Bluesy Shout, Baritone\n\nGritty, mid. The foundation is a heavy, driving drum beat and a powerful, overdriven electric guitar riff. The mood is determined, unrelenting, and gritty. A raw, powerful, and soulful male baritone sings with the force of a man engaged in hard labor.\n\nWe often see obstacles as interruptions to our life. This song argues that the obstacle is the life. Exploring the principle \"The Obstacle is the Way,\" the lyrics follow a mason who realizes the heavy stones blocking his path are actually the material he needs to build his character. It is a gritty anthem for transforming struggle into strength.\n\n\n    \n\n\n@TheShadyRiverBard",
      "clean_lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nThey put a wall up in my way\nA thousand stones of \"no you can't\"\nThe sun beat down on it all day\nA shadow where I'd meant to plant\nYeah, first I cursed and then I cried\nAnd looked for cracks to squeeze on through\nI beat it 'til my knuckles cried\nAnd didn't know what else to do\n\n[Chorus]\nBut this ain't the thing that blocks the path\nThis is the quarry and the stone\nIt ain't the focus of God's wrath\nIt's building me from skin and bone\nI am the mason of the wall\nAnd with each stone I stand up tall\nMy spirit's forged in sweat and fall\nYeah, I'm the mason of the wall\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe easy path is overgrown\nIt disappeared behind the haze\nI'm left here with these blocks of stone\nTo occupy my working days\nSo I picked up my calloused hands\nMixed mortar with my sweat and grit\nThe world can keep its promised lands\n'Cause I'm still building, bit by bit\n\n[Chorus]\n'Cause this ain't the thing that blocks the path\nThis is the quarry and the stone\nIt ain't the focus of God's wrath\nIt's building me from skin and bone\nI am the mason of the wall\nAnd with each stone I stand up tall\nMy spirit's forged in sweat and fall\nYeah, I'm the mason of the wall\n\n[Bridge]\nThe strain that breaks your back in two\nIs the same that makes the muscle grow\nThe hardest thing they make you do\nIs the only way you'll ever know\n\n[Chorus]\nNo, this ain't the thing that blocks the path\nThis is the quarry and the stone\nIt ain't the focus of God's wrath\nIt's building me from skin and bone\nI am the mason of the wall\nAnd with each stone I stand up tall\nMy spirit's forged in sweat and fall\nYeah, I'm the mason of the wall\n\n[Outro]\nThe stone! The fire! The skin! The bone!\nThe stone! The fire! The skin! The bone!\n\n\u00a9 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
