      "style": "Act II: The ForgeThe Obstacle is the WayTrack 07 of 13Tempo: Mid-tempo, steady and flowing07. Crooked Path, True North Hopeful Folk Rock, Americana, Heartland Rock \u2022 Mood: Reflective, Wise, Hopeful, Grateful, OptimisticOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "tempo": "Act II: The ForgeThe Obstacle is the WayTrack 07 of 13 Mid-tempo, steady and flowing07. Crooked Path, True NorthStyle: Hopeful Folk Rock, Americana, Heartland Rock \u2022 Mood: Reflective, Wise, Hopeful, Grateful, OptimisticOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "quote": "But every stumble, every fall\nAnd every time I thought I'd lost the way\nWas just a compass, after all\nPointing me right here to this day",
      "story": "\"Crooked Path, True North\" serves as the reflective conclusion to the album's second act, \"The Forge.\" This hopeful folk-rock track offers a final perspective on the principle \"The Obstacle is the Way,\" told from the viewpoint of someone looking back on a difficult life journey. The narrator recounts the detours, dead ends, and failures not as mistakes, but as the necessary, crooked path that ultimately revealed his \"true north\"\u2014his authentic self and purpose. The song's intricate acoustic picking and soaring, melodic feel provide a sense of clarity and gratitude, celebrating the hard-won wisdom that can only be gained through adversity.\n\nIntricate acoustic guitar picking, clean electric guitar, steady bass and drums, subtle organ pads \u2022 Male, Warm, Clear, Wise, Calm, Baritone\n\nHopeful, melodic Folk Rock with a strong Americana feel. The song is built on an intricate, driving fingerpicked acoustic guitar pattern. The mood is reflective and wise, building to a feeling of hope and gratitude. A warm, clear, and knowing lead male vocal tells the story of a life's journey.\n\nWe often regret our detours, but what if they were the only way to find the destination? This reflective song looks back on a life of mistakes\u2014failed farms, lost loves\u2014not with shame, but with gratitude. It suggests that getting \"good and lost\" was the necessary prerequisite for finding one's \"True North.\"\n\n\n    \n\n\n@TheShadyRiverBard",
      "clean_lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nI thought I had a perfect map\nA straight line drawn from A to B\nA fool who'd never seen the trap\nThat waits for plans made foolishly\nGot tangled in the briar patch\nOf youthful pride and wanting more\nPulled a latch on a dead-end hatch\nAnd wondered what I was living for\n\n[Chorus]\nBut every stumble, every fall\nAnd every time I thought I'd lost the way\nWas just a compass, after all\nPointing me right here to this day\nThe bitter taste, the heavy cost\nThe lessons written in the frost\nIt took the getting good and lost\nTo find my true north path\n\n[Verse 2]\nThat failed farm down by the creek\nWhere all I raised was doubt and debt\nIt taught me how to hear the meek\nA lesson I have not failed yet\nThat love that burned me to the ground\nAnd left a scar across my soul\nIt's where the seeds of grace were found\nWhen I learned to let go of control\n\n[Chorus]\n'Cause every stumble, every fall\nAnd every time I thought I'd lost the way\nWas just a compass, after all\nPointing me right here to this day\nThe bitter taste, the heavy cost\nThe lessons written in the frost\nIt took the getting good and lost\nTo find my true north path\n\n[Bridge]\nYou can't learn mountains on a plain\nYou can't know the sun without the rain\nEvery scar just proves the cost\nYou're never found until you're lost\n\n[Chorus]\nYeah, every stumble, every fall\nAnd every time I thought I'd lost the way\nWas just a compass, after all\nPointing me right here to this day\nThe bitter taste, the heavy cost\nThe lessons written in the frost\nIt took the getting good and lost\nTo find my true north path\n\n[Outro]\nMy crooked path, my true north\nMy crooked path, my true north\n\n\u00a9 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
