      "style": "Act III: The ReckoningMemento MoriTrack 09 of 13Tempo: Mid-tempo, walking pace09. The Unwritten Page Mid-tempo Country Blues, Folk, Americana \u2022 Mood: Urgent but not anxious, Reflective, Soulful, HopefulOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "tempo": "Act III: The ReckoningMemento MoriTrack 09 of 13 Mid-tempo, walking pace09. The Unwritten PageStyle: Mid-tempo Country Blues, Folk, Americana \u2022 Mood: Urgent but not anxious, Reflective, Soulful, HopefulOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "quote": "But right here is the unwritten page\nThe ink is wet, the pen is mine\nTo write a line upon life's stage\nA single, true, and honest line",
      "story": "Following the peaceful acceptance of \"The Final Acre,\" \"The Unwritten Page\" explores the urgent, practical implications of Memento Mori. This soulful country-blues track uses the metaphor of a life as a book: the past is filled with unchangeable, written pages, while the future remains a blank mystery. This awareness inspires the narrator to focus with clear-eyed purpose on the only thing he can control: the single, \"unwritten page\" of the present day. Driven by a steady mid-tempo rhythm and a soulful harmonica, the song is a vulnerable yet determined call to live consciously and virtuously in the here and now.\n\nSoulful harmonica, steady acoustic rhythm guitar, simple bass, light drums \u2022 Male, Vulnerable, Honest, Weathered, baritone\n\nA soulful, mid. The mood is reflective and urgent, but not anxious. A prominent, soulful harmonica weaves through the track, supported by a steady acoustic rhythm guitar. A vulnerable, honest, and weathered male baritone sings with a sense of clear.\n\nThe past is a book already written; the ink is dry. The future is a book not yet printed. The only thing we possess is the page open in front of us right now. This song uses the metaphor of authorship to explore agency and the present moment. It is a call to write a single, honest line today, regardless of what happened in the chapters before.\n\n\n    \n\n\n@TheShadyRiverBard",
      "clean_lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nThe book of me is worn and thumbed\nThe binding's cracked, the corners bent\nThe early chapters feel like from\nA life some other person spent\nThe ink is dry on every deed\nThe good, the bad, the in-between\nI can't go back and change a single read\nOr edit out a single scene\n\n[Chorus]\nBut right here is the unwritten page\nThe ink is wet, the pen is mine\nTo write a line upon life's stage\nA single, true, and honest line\nCan't change what's done, can't see the end\nSo I'll just live this day, my friend\nOn the unwritten page\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe pages yet to come are blank\nAnd blinding white under the sun\nFor every chapter I can thank\nThere could be ten, there could be none\nNo table of contents I can find\nNo epilogue to put me at ease\nJust this one moment for my mind\nTo catch the truth upon the breeze\n\n[Chorus]\n'Cause right here is the unwritten page\nThe ink is wet, the pen is mine\nTo write a line upon life's stage\nA single, true, and honest line\nCan't change what's done, can't see the end\nSo I'll just live this day, my friend\nOn the unwritten page\n\n[Bridge]\nSo will I write of fear or grace?\nOf holding grudges, letting go?\nThis page will be my time and place\nTo choose which kind of seeds I'll sow\n\n[Chorus]\nYeah, right here is the unwritten page\nThe ink is wet, the pen is mine\nTo write a line upon life's stage\nA single, true, and honest line\nCan't change what's done, can't see the end\nSo I'll just live this day, my friend\nOn the unwritten page\n\n[Outro]\nThe unwritten page\nWrite it now\n\n\u00a9 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
