      "tempo": "Act IV: The Unbroken ThreadSympatheiaTrack 11 of 13 Mid-to-up-tempo11. The River Runs Through AllStyle: Expansive Americana, Uplifting Folk Rock, Anthem \u2022 Mood: Hopeful, Joyful, Unifying, Anthemic, Awe-filled, CelebratoryOfficial VideoDrop a note to the bardShare this trackLyrics & Chords",
      "quote": "And oh, the river runs through all\nThe tangled roots, the concrete wall\nOne single drop contains the call\nOf every sea and every squall",
      "story": "\"The River Runs Through All\" opens the album's final act as its anthemic centerpiece, a soaring celebration of the Stoic principle of Sympatheia. Using the powerful metaphor of a river that connects diverse landscapes, the song explores the fundamental interconnectedness of all humanity and nature. It breaks down the artificial divides of politics, geography, and belief to reveal a shared, underlying current of existence. With its expansive Americana sound, driven by piano, a soaring fiddle, and rich vocal harmonies, the track serves as the album's most joyful and unifying statement, transforming the personal resilience cultivated in earlier acts into a profound sense of collective belonging.\n\nPiano, Fiddle, Acoustic Guitar, Electric Guitar, Bass, Drums, lush vocal harmonies \u2022 Male Baritone\n\nThe Stoic concept of Sympatheia teaches that \"all things are interwoven.\" This anthem celebrates that connection using the metaphor of a river that touches every shore\u2014mountain, city, farm, and sea. It is a rejection of artificial borders and a reminder that the same current flows through the veins of every living thing.\n\n\n    \n\n\n@TheShadyRiverBard",
      "clean_lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nIt starts as a whisper in the snow\nA single drop on granite high\nA tear of joy you'll never know\nFrom some forgotten passerby\nIt carves a path down through the stone\nIt doesn't ask which way to go\nIt never has to flow alone\nA patient and a steady flow\n\n[Chorus]\nAnd oh, the river runs through all\nThe tangled roots, the concrete wall\nOne single drop contains the call\nOf every sea and every squall\nThere is no great, there is no small\nNo final curtain, no last call\nJust listen, you can hear it fall\nThe river runs through all\n\n[Verse 2]\nIt cools the fields the farmer plows\n\nReflects the sweat upon his brows\nAnd helps his final harvest grow\nIt washes clean the city street\nThe rust and bone of what has been\nThe rhythm for a million feet\nThe sinner and the next of kin\n\n[Chorus]\nAnd oh, the river runs through all\nThe tangled roots, the concrete wall\nOne single drop contains the call\nOf every sea and every squall\nThere is no great, there is no small\nNo final curtain, no last call\nJust listen, you can hear it fall\nThe river runs through all\n\n[Bridge] (Revised)\nThe very water in the sea\nIs in the blood of you and me\nIt knows no borders, flags or lines\nJust how this one great current twines\n\n[Chorus]\nAND OH, THE RIVER RUNS THROUGH ALL\nTHE TANGLED ROOTS, THE CONCRETE WALL\nONE SINGLE DROP CONTAINS THE CALL\nOF EVERY SEA AND EVERY SQUALL\nTHERE IS NO GREAT, THERE IS NO SMALL\nNO FINAL CURTAIN, NO LAST CALL\nJUST LISTEN, YOU CAN HEAR IT FALL\nTHE RIVER RUNS THROUGH ALL\n\n[Outro]\nThe river runs through all\nThrough all of us\n\n\u00a9 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
